Q: How to get degrees by Accelerometer data (Java libGDX) A: <p>I have used the following solve in my libGDX app:</p>
<pre><code>            float x = Gdx.input.getAccelerometerX();
            float y = Gdx.input.getAccelerometerY();
            double rad = Math.atan2(y, x);
            double degrees = (Math.toDegrees(rad) + 360) % 360;
</code></pre>

Q: How to send dynamic comma separated string value in URL? A: <p>I assume the values are stored in array. You can create the string by joining array values with commas and then encode it for the URL.</p>
<pre><code>const commaSeparatedString = values.join(',');
const encodedString = encodeURIComponent(commaSeparatedString);

const url = `http://shopping.com/app/site/backend/additemtocart.nl?param=${encodedString}`;
</code></pre>

Q: How to refresh a div without reloading the entire page? A: <pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
$(document).ready(function () {
    // will call refreshPartial every 5 seconds
    setInterval(refreshPartial, 5000)

});

// calls action refreshing the partial
function refreshPartial() {
  $.ajax({
    url: "page_url",
    dataType: 'script',
    format: 'js'
 })
}
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
